            0.048,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Exploring Some Geometric Themes"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.09,
            0.35,
            0.111
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Koch Snowflake"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.112,
            0.847,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": "The Koch Snowflake is another fractal, named after the Swedish mathematician Von Koch, who first described it in 1904. We have already encountered this fractal in Grade 6, Ganita Prakash."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.195,
            0.321,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.218,
                0.311,
                0.269,
                0.327
              ],
              "content": "Step 0"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.191,
            0.544,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.441,
                0.311,
                0.49,
                0.327
              ],
              "content": "Step 1"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.618,
            0.189,
            0.767,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.661,
                0.311,
                0.712,
                0.327
              ],
              "content": "Step 2"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.428,
            0.356,
            0.593,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.431,
                0.475,
                0.555,
                0.492
              ],
              "content": "Koch Snowflake"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.516,
            0.77,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "To generate it, we start with an equilateral triangle. Each side is"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.54,
            0.532,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "(i) divided into 3 equal parts, and"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.564,
            0.845,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": "(ii) an equilateral triangle is raised over the middle part, and then the middle part is removed."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.606,
            0.847,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": "Effectively, each side gets replaced by a ‘bump’ - shaped structure . This procedure is repeated on the sides of the new resulting shape, and so on."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.672,
            0.294,
            0.694
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.697,
            0.846,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": "1. Draw the initial few steps (at least till Step 2) of the shape sequence that leads to the Koch Snowflake."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.745,
            0.847,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "2. Find the number of sides in the nth step of the shape sequence that leads to the Koch Snowflake."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.793,
            0.845,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": "3. Find the perimeter of the shape at the nth step of the sequence. Take the starting equilateral triangle to have a sidelength of 1 unit."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.876,
            0.913,
            0.91,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": "73"
        }
      ]
    }
